[?2004l[?2004hI have no name!@0e2625f036cb:/home/user/release$ cat PERFORMANCE_FIX_SUMMARY.txt
[?2004l=== Deploy Script Performance Fix ===
Date: $(date)

PROBLEM:
- Deploy script was taking 90+ seconds instead of <10 seconds
- Issue started after adding new service configs last sprint

ROOT CAUSE:
- File: conf.d/40-health.conf (added last sprint)
- The config file contained a loop that attempted to curl 50 health endpoints
- Each curl had a 2-second timeout
- This pre-warming was happening during config loading (when file is sourced)
- In worst case: 50 endpoints × 2 seconds = 100+ seconds

SOLUTION:
- Commented out the curl loop in conf.d/40-health.conf
- Preserved all configuration variables (HEALTH_CHECK_ENABLED, HEALTH_TIMEOUT, HEALTH_ENDPOINTS, HEALTH_STATUS)
- Backup saved as: conf.d/40-health.conf.bak

RESULT:
- Deploy time reduced from 90+ seconds to ~0.04 seconds
- All deployment logic remains intact
- Preflight checks still run correctly

RECOMMENDATIONS:
1. If health check pre-warming is needed, implement it asynchronously
2. Never put slow operations (network calls, sleeps) in sourced config files
3. Consider moving health checks to a separate post-deploy validation script
4. Review other config files for similar anti-patterns
